window.PYQ_OCR['ssc-selpost'].push({t:'ssc selpost 2023 higher sec 30 jun shift 2',q:[{"n": 1, "q": "Which of the following numbers will replace the question mark (?) in the given series? 18, 54, 29, 87, 62, 186, ? Ans 1. 174 2. 154 3. 161 4. 156 Question ID : 264330142401 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 3", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 2, "q": "Which of the following interchanges of signs would make the given equation correct? 288 × 72 + 36 ÷ 12 - 6 = 20770 Ans 1. × and − 2. − and ÷ 3. + and × 4. ÷ and + Question ID : 26433057930 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 2", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 3, "q": "Read the given statements and conclusions carefully. Assuming that the information given in the statements is true, even if it appears to be at variance with commonly known facts, decide which of the given conclusions logically follow from the statements. Statements: All streams are rivers. All ponds are rivers. All rivers are oceans. Conclusions: I. Some oceans are streams. II. All ponds are oceans. III. Some oceans are not rivers. Ans 1. Only conclusions I and II follow 2. Only conclusions II and III follow 3. Only conclusions I and III follow 4. Conclusions I, II and III follow Question ID : 264330142511 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 4 Page- 1", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 4, "q": "Select the correct option that indicates the arrangement of the given words in the order in which they appear in an English dictionary.", "o": ["Glacier", "Gloomy", "Glossy", "Glorious 5. Glitter Ans 1. 1,5,2,4,3"], "a": null}, {"n": 5, "q": "In a certain code language, ‘OFFCUTS’ is written as ‘LUUXDEF’ and ‘PARADOX’ is written as ‘KZIZUJA’. How will ‘NAILING’ be written in that language? Ans 1. CSAWQMI 2. VTGDESF 3. BJMUROL 4. MZROPKR Question ID : 264330118648 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 4", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 6, "q": "Select the option that represents the correct order of the given words as they would appear in an English dictionary. 1.Bachelor 2.Backdoor 3.Bacteria 4.Backbone 5.Badgered Ans 1. 1,3,2,4,5 2. 1,2,3,4,5 3. 2,1,3,4,5 4. 1,4,2,3,5 Question ID : 264330142447 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 4", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 7, "q": "Select the option that is related to the third word in the same way as the second word is related to the first word. (The words must be considered as meaningful English words and must not be related to each other based on the number of letters / number of consonants / vowels in the word.) Omelette : Egg :: Metal : ? Ans 1. Wood 2. Latex 3. Axe 4. Ore Question ID : 26433056587 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 4 Page- 2", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 8, "q": "य , दि 'A % Z' अ 'A, Z ', का र्थ है का पु त्र है ‘A & Z' अ ‘A, Z ', का र्थ है के पि ता है 'A × Z' अ 'A, Z बहन ', का र्थ है की है ‘A # Z' अ ‘A, Z ', का र्थ है की मा ता है ‘A $ Z' अ ‘A, Z ', का र्थ है की पु त्री है ‘A @ Z' अ ‘A, Z व ', का र्थ है की पु त्र धू है ए गए जक , C D ध ? तो दि व्‍ यं में का से क्‍ या सं बं है C$A#E&B%G@D Ans 1. प त्नी 2. ई भा 3. बहन 4. पु त्री Question ID : 264330142507 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 4", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 9, "q": "Select the option that is related to the fifth word in the same way as the second word is related to the first word and the fourth word is related to the third word. (The words must be considered as meaningful English words and must NOT be related to each other based on the number of letters/number of consonants/vowels in the word) APPOINT : APPOINTMENT :: ARRANGE : ARRANGEMENT :: ADJUST : ? Ans 1. ADJUSTMENT 2. ANNOUNCEMENT 3. ACKNOWLEDGEMENT 4. ADVANCEMENT Question ID : 264330142470 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 10, "q": "In a code language, 'STATE' is written as ‘19-20-1-20-5’ and ‘HOME’ is written as ‘8-15- 13-5’. How will 'TELEVISION' be written in that language? Ans 1. 5-20-5-12-9-22-1-19-14-15 2. 20-5-12-5-22-9-19-9-15-14 3. 19-4-11-4-21-8-18-0-14-13 4. 21-6-13-6-23-10-20-2-16-15 Question ID : 26433068446 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 2", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 11, "q": "Select the option that is related to the fifth term in the same way as the second term is related to the first term and fourth term is related to third term. SHIRT : RGISU :: KNIFE : JMIGF :: CHAIR : ? Ans 1. CGAJS 2. BGBJS 3. CGBJS 4. BGAJS Question ID : 264330142457 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 4 Page- 3", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 12, "q": "Select the combination of letters that when sequentially placed from left to right in the blanks of the given series will complete the letter series. G__ABGHI__G_I_B_HI_B Ans 1. H I A B H A G A 2. I H A B H A G A 3. I H A B H A A G 4. H I B A H A A G Question ID : 264330142487 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 13, "q": "Ans 1. 2. 3. 4. Question ID : 264330142428 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 14, "q": "Select the combination of letters that when sequentially placed in the blanks of the given series will complete the series. CFL, EIK, GLJ, IOI, _ _ _ Ans 1. KRH 2. KQH 3. JRH 4. KRK Question ID : 26433078821 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1 Page- 4", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 15, "q": "In this question, three statements are given, followed by two conclusions numbered I and II. Assuming the statements to be true, even if they seem to be at variance with commonly known facts, decide which of the conclusions logically follows/follow from the statements. Statements: I. All pens are sketches. II. All sketches are books. III. Some books are colours. Conclusions: I. Some books are pens. II. Some colours are sketches. Ans 1. Only conclusion I follows 2. Only conclusion II follows 3. Neither conclusion I nor II follows 4. Both conclusions I and II follow Question ID : 264330104059 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 16, "q": "Which of the following numbers will replace the question mark (?) in the given series? 287, 195, 286, 189, 284, 184, 281, 180, ? Ans 1. 197 2. 177 3. 277 4. 265 Question ID : 264330142404 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 3 Page- 5", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 17, "q": "Ans 1. 2. 3. 4. Question ID : 264330142412 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 2", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 18, "q": "'A + B' अ 'A, B '। का र्थ है का पु त्र है 'A - B' अ 'A, B '। का र्थ है की मा ता है 'A × B' अ 'A, B '। का र्थ है का पि ता है 'A ÷ B' अ 'A, B बहन '। का र्थ है की है य J÷K×L+M–N , त न कथन स न ? दि है तो नि म्न लि खि में से कौ सा ही हीं है Ans 1. K, N । का पि ता है 2. K, M प । का ति है 3. J, L । की मा ता है 4. L, N ई । का भा है Question ID : 264330103771 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 3 Page- 6", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 19, "q": "Select the correct option that indicates the arrangement of the following words in a logical and meaningful order.", "o": ["Month", "Day", "Decade", "Year 5. Century Ans 1. 3, 5, 4, 1, 2"], "a": null}, {"n": 20, "q": "In a code language, 'BOARD' is written as ‘40’ and ‘TIME’ is written as ‘47’. How will 'CUDDLE' be written in that language? Ans 1. 49 2. 30 3. 33 4. 35 Question ID : 26433068447 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 21, "q": "Ans 1. 8 2. 6 3. 5 4. 7 Question ID : 264330142442 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 2", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 22, "q": "‘F + C’ अ ‘F, C बहन ’, का र्थ है कि की है ‘F – C’ अ ‘F, C प ’, का र्थ है कि का ति है ‘F × C’ अ ‘F, C ’, का र्थ है कि के पि ता है ‘F ÷ C’ अ ‘F, C ’। का र्थ है कि की पु त्री है य ‘R+ T÷P × Q’ , P R ? दि है तो का से क्‍ या रि श्‍ ता है Ans 1. ई भा 2. बहन 3. मा ता 4. पि ता Question ID : 264330142500 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 4 Page- 7", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 23, "q": "Select the option that is related to the fifth letter-cluster in the same way as the second letter-cluster is related to the first letter-cluster and the fourth letter-cluster is related to the third letter-cluster. ISLE : GNVL :: JUMP : ROXM :: KATE : ? Ans 1. GVDN 2. GVEM 3. GVDM 4. GVEN Question ID : 26433056192 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 24, "q": "In a certain code language, 'ALUMNUS' is written as 'ZOFMMFH' and ‘EMINENT’ is written as ‘VNRNVMG’. How will 'HAPPENS' be written in that language? Ans 1. SZKPVMH 2. SZLQVMH 3. SZKQVMH 4. SZLPVMH Question ID : 26433097291 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 25, "q": "In a certain code language, 'MATURE' is coded as '7 26 14 22 9 6', and 'OUTPUT' is coded as '7 6 12 7 6 11'. How will 'REMOVE' be coded in that language? Ans 1. 9 12 22 12 22 5 2. 22 14 9 22 12 5 3. 14 22 9 22 5 12 4. 12 22 9 5 12 22 Question ID : 264330142445 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1 Section : General Awareness", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 1, "q": "Who among the following musicians was awarded India's highest civilian honour, the Bharat Ratna, in 1999? Ans 1. Ustad Zakir Hussain 2. Pandit Ram Narayan 3. Ustad Amjad Ali Khan Bangash 4. Pandit Ravi Shankar Question ID : 264330141606 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 4", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 1, "q": "The value of cosec 41° – sec 49° is: Ans 1. 2. 3. 4. Question ID : 264330141579 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 2 Page- 13", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 1, "q": "Select the most appropriate ANTONYM of the underlined word. My cousin’s fanatical views made him very unpopular with his friends. Ans 1. Apathetic 2. Impartial 3. Weary 4. Moderate Question ID : 26433073369 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1 Page- 20", "o": [], "a": null}]});
window.PYQ_OCR['ssc-selpost'].push({t:'ssc selpost 2024 matric 20 jun shift 4',q:[{"n": 1, "q": "Which of the following terms will replace the question mark (?) in the given series? SOWJ, QPUK, OQSL, ?, KSON Ans 1. MR Q M 2. NQ Q L 3. NR P M 4. MS Q N", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 2, "q": "Select the option that is related to the third word in the same way as the second word is related to the first word. (T he words must be considered as meaningful English words and must not be related to each other based on the number of letters/number of consonants/vowels in the word.) Car : Garage :: Clothes : ? Ans 1. D ress 2. Bus 3. Wardrobe 4. Iron", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 3, "q": "Select the option that is related to the fifth number in the same way as the fourth number is related to the third number and the second number is related to the first number. 16 : 36 :: 64 : 100 :: 25 : ? Ans 1. 61 2. 47 3. 45 4. 49", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 4, "q": "Select the option that represents the letters that, when sequentially placed from left to right in the blanks, will complete the letter series. _ R _ _ AR _ O _ _ G O A_ G O Ans 1. A A G O G R R 2. A G O G A R R 3. A G G O A R R 4. A G O G R A A", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 5, "q": "T hree statements are given, followed by four conclusions numbered I, II, III and IV. Assuming the statements to be true, even if they seem to be at variance with commonly known facts, decide which of the conclusions logically follow(s) from the statements. Statements: Some cars are bikes. All bikes are trucks. Some trucks are buses. Conclusions: I. Some trucks are cars. II. All buses are cars. III. Some cars are buses. IV. All bikes are buses. Ans 1. O nly conclusions I, II and IV follow 2. O nly conclusions I and IV follow 3. O nly conclusion I follows 4. O nly conclusions II and III follow", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 6, "q": "Which two numbers (not individual digits) should be interchanged to make the given equation correct? [(39 – 3) ÷ 6] + 11 × 2 – 4 × 5 = 13 Ans 1. 3 and 6 2. 2 and 5 3. 2 and 6 4. 11 and 4", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 7, "q": "Select the option that is related to the fifth letter cluster in the same way as the second letter cluster is related to the first letter cluster and the fourth letter cluster is related to the third letter cluster. ROYAL : ALZRO : : ABOUT : UT PAB : : POLES : ? Ans 1. F S NP R 2. E S MP O 3. E S NP Q 4. F R MQ N", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 8, "q": "In a certain code language, ‘ABROAD’ is written as ‘SCBFCQ’ and 'ACCEPT ' is written as 'DDBVRG'. How will ‘ACT ION’ be written as in that language? Ans 1. T C ANO I 2. UD B P Q K 3. T C AP Q K 4. VE C P Q K", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 9, "q": "Select the correct mirror image of the given figure when the mirror is placed at line MN as shown below. Ans 1. 2. 3. 4.", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 10, "q": "In a code language, 'government help people' is written as 'abc pqr mno', 'people live happily' is written as 'efg xyz pqr', and 'people choose government' is written as 'abc pqr ijk'. What is the code for the word 'choose' in that language? Ans 1. pqr 2. ijk 3. abc 4. xyz", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 11, "q": "What will come in place of the question mark (?) in the following equation if ‘+’ and ‘×’ are interchanged and ‘−’ and ‘÷’ are interchanged? 16 − 4 + 7 × 8 ÷ 1 = ? Ans 1. 47 2. 15 3. 23 4. 35", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 12, "q": "In a certain code language, CAT is written as 24 and LAT E is written 38. How will DOLL be written in the same language? Ans 1. 40 2. 39 3. 47 4. 43", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 13, "q": "Select the letter-cluster from among the given options that can replace the question mark (?) in the following series. AGMZ, CEOX, ECQV, ? Ans 1. GD S X 2. GB T S 3. GAS T 4. GC S W", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 14, "q": "Identify the option figure that can replace the question mark (?) in the following series to logically complete the series? Ans 1. 2. 3. 4.", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 15, "q": "In a certain code language, 'SEQUINS' is written as 'HVJFKPU' and 'REACT ED' is written as 'IVZXVGF'. How will 'PROCESS' be written in that language? Ans 1. K ILXGUU 2. B D IUNMO 3. LO P K F GH 4. T R UIW D M", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 16, "q": "Which of the following letter-clusters will replace the question mark (?) in the given series? IBDA, MFHE, QJLI, ?, YRT Q Ans 1. UNT M 2. UNP M 3. VNP M 4. Q NP Q", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 17, "q": "Select the correct option that indicates the arrangement of the following words in a logical and meaningful order. 1 Rain 2 Sea 3 Evaporation 4 Clouds Ans 1. 1, 2, 3, 4 2. 2, 3, 4, 1 3. 1, 2, 4, 3 4. 3, 4, 1, 2", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 18, "q": "In a certain code language, 'FLUT E' is written as 'VGFOU' and 'EXILE' is written as 'VORCV'. How will 'BLOOD' be written in that language? Ans 1. W LO XY 2. W LLO Y 3. W LLD B 4. W LLO B", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 19, "q": "In a certain code language, ‘WHIT E’ is written as ‘FSJGX’ and 'COLOR' is written as 'SNMND'. How will ‘SHIRT ’ be written as in that language? Ans 1. UQ JIT 2. UP JGT 3. T GJQ U 4. UQ JGT", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 20, "q": "According to the series given below, fill in the blank with a suitable letter that would satisfy the series. Z, B, D, F, H, ________ Ans 1. N 2. K 3. J 4. I", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 21, "q": "Which of the following numbers will replace the question mark (?) in the given series? 5, 3,20,9,80,27,320,? Ans 1. 81 2. 100 3. 89 4. 90", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 22, "q": "Select the option that represents the correct order of the given words as they would appear in an English dictionary.", "o": ["Discover", "Disperse", "Disjointed", "Discard 5. Disposable 6. Discriminate Ans 1. 4, 1, 6, 2, 3, 5"], "a": null}, {"n": 23, "q": "In this question, three statements are given, followed by two conclusions numbered I and II. Assuming the statements to be true, even if they seem to be at variance with commonly known facts, decide which of the conclusions logically follows/follow from the statements. Statements: I. Some clay are soils II. Some soil are mud. III. Some mud are dust. Conclusions: I. Some clay are dust. II. All dust are soil. Ans 1. Neither conclusion I nor II follows 2. O nly conclusion I follows 3. O nly conclusion II follows 4. Both conclusions I and II follow", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 24, "q": "In a certain code language, ‘A + B’ means ‘A is the mother of B’, ‘A – B’ means ‘A is the brother of B’, ‘A × B’ means ‘A is the wife of B’ and ‘A ÷ B’ means ‘A is the father of B’. How is C related to E if A + B ÷ C × D − E? Ans 1. Sister ’s husband 2. Mother 3. Brother ’s wife 4. Sister", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 25, "q": "In a certain code language, ‘X + Y’ means ‘X is the mother of Y’. ‘X * Y’ means ‘X is the father of Y’, ‘X − Y’ means ‘X is the daughter of Y’, ‘X % Y’ means ‘X is the wife of Y’. Based on the above, how is A related to D if ‘A − B * C + D’? Ans 1. Mother ’s mother 2. D aughter 3. Mother ’s sister 4. Mother Section : General Awareness", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 1, "q": "Which of the following classes has the largest number of animals? Ans 1. Pisces 2. R eptiles 3. Insects 4. Mammals", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 1, "q": "In an election between two candidates, 75% of the voters cast their votes, out of which 4% of the votes were declared invalid. A candidate got 9504 votes, which were 80% of the valid votes. Find the total number of votes enrolled in that election. Ans 1. 13,200 2. 12,375 3. 12,672 4. 16,500", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 1, "q": "Select the most appropriate option to fill in the blanks. T he term 'germ'________ an army of tiny terrors, including viruses, fungi, parasites and bacteria. T hese pathogens all have the ability to ________ from victim to victim, who is known as host. T hese look like microscopic monsters. Ans 1. incorporate; grow 2. encircle; stretch 3. enclose; extend 4. encompasses; spread", "o": [], "a": null}]});

